up|towards-higher-place|ADVERB|Towards a higher place|Towards a position above the current or starting position.|lên; lên trên|The balloon floated up until it touched the ceiling.|Quả bóng bay lên cho đến khi chạm trần.|No noun complement is required; look up, climb up. Context distinguishes physical direction from other uses.|0
up|increase-in-level|ADVERB|Increase in level|To a greater amount, value or level.|tăng lên|The price of timber went up again this month.|Giá gỗ lại tăng lên trong tháng này.|Often with go or move; prices are up. The subject can be an abstract quantity.|1
up|towards-top-along-route|PREPOSITION|Towards the top along a route|Along a sloping or rising route towards its higher end.|lên; theo hướng lên|They carried the empty boxes up the stairs.|Họ mang những chiếc hộp rỗng lên cầu thang.|Followed by a route noun phrase: up the hill, up the stairs.|2
wage|pay-for-work|NOUN|Pay for work|Money paid to someone for their work, often calculated by the hour or week.|tiền công; tiền lương|The workshop pays a weekly wage to its assistants.|Xưởng trả lương hằng tuần cho các phụ tá.|Countable in a wage; wages is often plural for earnings. A salary is commonly a fixed regular annual amount.|0
carrot|orange-root-vegetable|NOUN|Root vegetable|A plant with an edible root, commonly long and orange, eaten as a vegetable.|cà rốt|He sliced a carrot into thin strips for the salad.|Anh ấy thái một củ cà rốt thành những sợi mỏng để làm salad.|Countable for individual roots; grated carrot can be uncountable as an ingredient. Some varieties have other colours.|0
fast|moving-quickly|ADJECTIVE|Moving quickly|Able to move or happen at a high speed.|nhanh|A fast train passed the small station without stopping.|Một chuyến tàu nhanh chạy qua ga nhỏ mà không dừng.|Fast, faster, fastest; describes a noun or follows be. This adjective does not use fastly.|0
fast|at-high-speed|ADVERB|At high speed|At a high speed or in a short time.|nhanh|The stream flowed fast after the heavy rain.|Dòng suối chảy nhanh sau trận mưa lớn.|Same form as the adjective; run fast, work faster. Do not use fastly.|1
fast|go-without-food|VERB|Go without food|To deliberately avoid eating for a period of time.|nhịn ăn|The character fasted for a day as part of a religious observance.|Nhân vật nhịn ăn một ngày theo một nghi thức tôn giáo.|Usually intransitive; fast for a period. Fasting is the activity; this lexical example does not recommend a practice.|-
kin|family-relatives|NOUN|Family relatives|People related to a person by family ties.|họ hàng; người thân|She stayed with her kin while the house was repaired.|Cô ấy ở cùng người thân trong lúc căn nhà được sửa.|Collective noun, often literary or formal; next of kin names the closest relative or relatives.|-
